	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div>
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>Non clam te est omnes angulos <persName>Momis</persName>, <persName>Coriceis</persName><note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1">Lauscher; vgl. <bibl source="b56">Adagia</bibl>, 1, 2, 44 (<bibl source="b370">LB</bibl> II ...).</note> <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>et vitilitigatoribus esse refertissimos; ideo <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>nos paucis complectimur omnia verbis <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>proque muta vivam mittimus epistolam.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z5"/>Virgo, quae <placeName ref="l145">Esslingae</placeName> per quinquennium nescio quid <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>habuit in utero, 30. die octobris a senatu <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>in captivitatem cum parentibus, sorore et <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>custodibus coniecta est<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Anne Ulmerin; s. ZBZ, Ms F 22a, S. 349f (Bericht aus Esslingen vom 3. Nov. 1550), auch Ms. F 13 (S. ??); <hi>Fehr,</hi> Massenkunst 92 und Tafel 30/31; Lycosthenes, Prodigiorum et ostentorum chronicon, S. 592-594; Ulinka <hi>Rublack,</hi> Pregnancy, Childbirth and the Female Body in Early Modern Germany, in: Past and Present, Nr. 150, Feb. 1996, S. 84-110, hier S. 95f mit Anm. 50: "The Deceitful Woman of Esslingen", Zentralbibliothek <placeName ref="l587">Zurich</placeName>, Wickiana, PAS II 2/13, reproduced in The German Single Leaf Woodcut, 1500-1550, ed. M. Geisberg, rev. W. L. Strauss, 4 vols. (New York, 1974), iii, p. 1066, G. 1118; "Gruntliche antzaigung des Teufflischenn und schentlichen betrugs Mit dem gemachten Bauch von anfang biss zu end 1551", PAS II 10/19b; "Des falschen Weibs vnd Junckfrawen zu Esslingen Auss gericht" (undated), PAS 10/19; "Blut- oder Peinliches Urtelbuech", Staatsarchiv Ludwigsburg, B 169, Bu. 119 I, f. [145.sup.v]-[156.sup.r], 23 Jan. 1551.</note>.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Totam fere <placeName ref="l822">Germaniam</placeName>, <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>quemadmodum <persName>Laminitle</persName><note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">Anna Laminit; s. Roper, The Holy Household 262f.</note> quondam <persName>Augustanos</persName> <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>(si verum est, quod dicitur) decepit.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">Vale.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z11"/><placeName ref="l195">Gepingę</placeName> ex phrontisterio nostro 3. die <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>novembris anno 1550.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z13"/><persName ref="p8">Ioachim Aberlin</persName>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Eximio theologo <lb xml:id="p2z2"/><persName ref="p495">Heynricho Bullingero</persName> S.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
